// ============================================================================
// INCIDENT SCRATCHPAD // OSIRIS WORKSTATION // PROCESS REMEDIATION
// HOST: osiris-ws-01 | USER: morgan [SYSADMIN] | TIMESTAMP: 06:15:33 AM
// FILE: /tmp/NOTE.txt
// ============================================================================

Alice—

Our CPU thermal alarm is firing. The intruder dropped a persistent background
miner into /tmp (sys_miner) that is consuming nearly 100% of our compute cycles
and locking socket memory.

1. Inspect active processes:
   ps aux

2. Clear stalled audit tasks:
   kill 102

3. Watch out for uncooperative daemons: PID 104 traps Signal 15.
   Use non-maskable SIGKILL:
   kill -9 104

Kill the miner so our CPU cools down and frees up the network stack.

— Morgan
// ============================================================================

